// =============================================================================
// _tod_gameover.gsc — the GAME-OVER DECISION MENU (v9.24, user 2026-08-23: "We
// need a fast restart menu after a game loss. Or else this is just annoying
// that you have to go back and everything. The other map had something like
// this").
//
// Port of map 1's retry-on-death v3 (_acc_leaderboard.gsc::offer_retry_on_death
// + docs/40) WITHOUT the leaderboard plumbing. On end_game:
//   1. synchronously park stock's auto-exit — _zm.gsc::end_game reads
//      level.zombie_vars["zombie_intermission_time"] (stock 15s) at :6208,
//      long after the notify, then ExitLevel(false) at :6250;
//   2. after a 3s settle (the intermission camera cut + stock's GAME OVER /
//      "survived N rounds" text fade in behind), release the scoreboard stock
//      forced up at :6204 (LUINotifyEvent force_scoreboard 1,0 — stock's own
//      release call, :6244), set the host-side dvar tod_go_active=1,
//      RE-ENABLE the ingame menu stock disabled at :6043 (SetMatchFlag
//      disableIngameMenu 0 — that flag is the ONLY gate, which is itself the
//      proof the menu works at intermission) and force-open StartMenu_Main on
//      every player (OpenMenu, the stock builtin _zm.gsc:636);
//   3. AetheriumStartMenu.lua's dvar-gated game-over mode then shows exactly
//      two native up/down entries — RESTART MAP (Engine.Exec map_restart: the
//      pause menu's own Restart Level lane — a full script restart WITHOUT the
//      lobby round-trip) and END GAME (the Leave Game disconnect lane). Both
//      act from the menu itself and tear the VM down; nothing returns here.
//   4. no choice in TOD_GO_DECIDE_SECS -> ExitLevel(false), stock's terminal
//      call; an independent failsafe exits at TOD_GO_FAILSAFE_SECS if this
//      thread ever died; stock's own parked wait is the last net. The game can
//      never sit on the death screen forever.
//
// The dvar is HOST-machine only: co-op peers get the normal pause list (Leave
// Game works there; restarting is the host's call). Dvars persist across
// map_restart within one app session, so init SCRUBS it — a leftover "1"
// would turn the next game's mid-run pause menu into the two-entry list.
// This also fires after the FINALE's win (it ends via the same end_game) —
// Restart Map / End Game after escaping is the right offer there too.
// Solo note: an open menu pauses the server and freezes the countdown — by
// design (a player IN the menu is deciding, not AFK); ESC closes it like any
// pause menu and ESC reopens it (the ingame menu stays enabled).
// NO dev dvars and no live-disable switch — ship behavior (map doctrine).
// =============================================================================
#using scripts\shared\util_shared;
#using scripts\zm\zm_tod2_cybercity\_tod_gauge;   // tier_progress / tier_floor_display (the loss screen's floor readout)
#insert scripts\shared\shared.gsh;

// THE LOSS BANNER (PK09, 2026-10-04) - GENERATED by tools/artgen/packs/pk09_loss_banner.py, the
// win banner's twin. A hudelem SetShader takes a MATERIAL (the 2d_blend wrapping i_tod_lose_banner).
#precache( "material", "tod_lose_banner" );

#namespace tod_gameover;

#define TOD_GO_STOCK_PARK_SECS   120   // stock's intermission wait, stretched behind our window
#define TOD_GO_DECIDE_SECS       60    // no choice in this long -> auto End Game
#define TOD_GO_FAILSAFE_SECS     90    // independent watchdog (main <=63s, this 90s, stock ~120s)

// THE LOSS SCREEN'S GEOMETRY (PK09). The banner is the win banner's size (2048x512 art drawn at
// 4:1); pk09_loss_banner.py --check fails if these lose the art's aspect.
#define TOD_GO_BANNER_W          900
#define TOD_GO_BANNER_H          225
#define TOD_GO_BANNER_SPLIT_W    600   // splitscreen: half the vertical room (the finale's numbers)
#define TOD_GO_BANNER_SPLIT_H    150
// The baked readout plate's centre, as a fraction of the banner's DRAWN height below the banner's
// centre. LOCKSTEP pk09_loss_banner.py READOUT_CY: ( 422 - 256 ) / 512. --check fails on a drift.
#define TOD_GO_READOUT_FRAC      0.32421875
// The live floor text inside that plate. The plate's inside is ~210 x 30 units at 900x225; every
// string lost_game_over can print is 9 characters at most ("FLOOR 50", "UNDERCITY", "THE CROWN").
#define TOD_GO_FLOOR_SCALE       2
#define TOD_GO_FLOOR_SCALE_SPLIT 1.5
#define TOD_GO_FLOOR_GLOW        0.3   // the red halo round the readout text; 0 = none
// Below the banner, as on the win screen (user 2026-08-25: the survived line "overlaps with the new
// asset" at stock's -100). The banner covers y -242..-18; +40 clears it.
#define TOD_GO_SURVIVED_Y        40

function init()
{
	SetDvar( "tod_go_active", "" );   // stale-dvar scrub (see header)
	// v16.3 — the LOSS screen carries the floor (see lost_game_over). Installed
	// at init; the WIN path overwrites it at its own moment
	// (_tod_finale escaped_game_over).
	level.custom_game_over_hud_elem = &lost_game_over;
	level thread offer_restart_on_end();
	level thread gameover_failsafe();
}

// Stock _zm::end_game calls this per player INSTEAD of its own game_over /
// survived setup when it is defined ( player, game_over_elem, survived_elem ),
// then sets the survived text + fade itself (the same contract
// _tod_finale::escaped_game_over rides). This is the LOSS screen.
//
// PK09 (2026-10-04): BAKED ART, LIKE THE WIN SCREEN. Until then this drew
// "GAME OVER  -  FLOOR N" in the stock hudelem font while the only end-screen
// art in the map belonged to the parked finale. Now game_over draws the
// GAME OVER banner (tod_lose_banner, the win banner's chassis in the
// synthwave UI palette: a dead stair, a dead grid, GAME OVER in the map's
// typeface), and the floor - the map's headline number at the one moment
// players screenshot (repo review 2026-09-01) - is LIVE text on its own elem,
// laid into the banner's empty readout plate (a hudelem draws one shader OR
// one string, the emblem pattern in escaped_game_over). Stock writes the
// survived line's text itself after this returns, so the floor cannot ride it.
function lost_game_over( player, game_over, survived )
{
	split = player IsSplitScreen();
	bw = TOD_GO_BANNER_W;
	bh = TOD_GO_BANNER_H;
	if ( split )
	{
		bw = TOD_GO_BANNER_SPLIT_W;
		bh = TOD_GO_BANNER_SPLIT_H;
	}

	game_over.alignX = "center";
	game_over.alignY = "middle";
	game_over.horzAlign = "center";
	game_over.vertAlign = "middle";
	game_over.y -= 130;
	if ( split )
		game_over.y += 40;
	game_over.foreground = true;
	game_over.sort = 1;
	game_over.alpha = 0;
	// WHITE, so the art shows its own colours (SetShader tints by .color).
	game_over.color = ( 1, 1, 1 );
	game_over.hidewheninmenu = true;
	game_over SetShader( "tod_lose_banner", bw, bh );
	game_over FadeOverTime( 1 );
	game_over.alpha = 1;

	// THE FLOOR READOUT: its own elem, drawn OVER the banner (sort 2 > 1),
	// centred on the baked plate, fading in a beat after the banner.
	text = loss_readout();
	readout = NewClientHudElem( player );
	if ( isdefined( readout ) )
	{
		readout.alignX = "center";
		readout.alignY = "middle";
		readout.horzAlign = "center";
		readout.vertAlign = "middle";
		readout.x = 0;
		readout.y = game_over.y + TOD_GO_READOUT_FRAC * bh;
		readout.foreground = true;
		readout.sort = 2;
		readout.fontScale = TOD_GO_FLOOR_SCALE;
		if ( split )
			readout.fontScale = TOD_GO_FLOOR_SCALE_SPLIT;
		readout.color = ( 0.94, 0.95, 0.98 );   // RT: the Fallen white, red-lit (pk09 GSC_TINTS pins it to the banner's theme)
		readout.glowColor = ( 0.95, 0.13, 0.23 );
		readout.glowAlpha = TOD_GO_FLOOR_GLOW;
		readout.hidewheninmenu = true;
		readout.alpha = 0;
		readout SetText( text );
		readout FadeOverTime( 1.4 );
		readout.alpha = 1;
		level thread readout_cleanup( readout );
	}

	survived.alignX = "center";
	survived.alignY = "middle";
	survived.horzAlign = "center";
	survived.vertAlign = "middle";
	survived.y += TOD_GO_SURVIVED_Y;
	if ( split )
		survived.y += 40;
	survived.foreground = true;
	survived.fontScale = 2;
	if ( split )
		survived.fontScale = 1.5;
	survived.alpha = 0;
	survived.color = ( 0.52, 0.56, 0.67 );     // RT: the Fallen grey secondary text (docs/180 #858EAB)
	survived.hidewheninmenu = true;

	go_log( "LOSS player=" + player GetEntityNumber() + " readout=" + text + " split=" + split
	        + " banner=" + bw + "x" + bh + " y=" + game_over.y + " readout_y=" + ( game_over.y + TOD_GO_READOUT_FRAC * bh ) );
}

// -> the text in the banner's readout: how far the RUN got.
// THE CROWN while the party never left the crown island (_tod_fall's crown
// phase still holds), else the deepest floor anyone reached on the descent
// (the highest on the climb layout) - tier_progress is the floors of progress
// the layout counts and tier_floor_display turns progress back into a floor
// number, so this reads the same on either layout without knowing which one
// is live. Floor 0 is below the tower: the Undercity. Progress only ever
// rises, so a player who rode a teleporter back up keeps the floor he
// reached; the run is shared, so the party's best is the screen's number. A
// plain-string SetText mints one config string per distinct text - fine ONCE
// at end_game, and every player gets the same one.
function loss_readout()
{
	if ( IS_TRUE( level.tod_fall_phase ) )
		return "THE CROWN";
	best = 0;
	foreach ( p in GetPlayers() )
	{
		d = tod_gauge::tier_progress( p );
		if ( d > best )
			best = d;
	}
	f = tod_gauge::tier_floor_display( best );
	if ( f <= 0 )
		return "UNDERCITY";
	return "FLOOR " + f;
}

// Stock destroys its own two elems on "stop_intermission"; ours goes with them.
// (Our restart menu normally ends the level long before, which frees it anyway.)
function readout_cleanup( readout )
{
	level waittill( "stop_intermission" );
	if ( isdefined( readout ) )
		readout Destroy();
}

function go_log( msg )
{
	if ( !( IS_TRUE( level.tod_dev ) || IS_TRUE( level.tod_diag ) ) )
		return;
	line = "[TOD_GAMEOVER] ms=" + GetTime() + " " + msg;
	/#
	PrintLn( line );
	#/
}

// Deliberately NO endon("end_game") — this RUNS at end_game.
function offer_restart_on_end()
{
	level waittill( "end_game" );

	// Claim the frame synchronously on the notify: stock reads this value well
	// after it, so the 15s auto-exit is parked before it can ever be scheduled.
	level.zombie_vars[ "zombie_intermission_time" ] = TOD_GO_STOCK_PARK_SECS;

	wait 3;
	if ( GetPlayers().size == 0 )
		return;

	// Release the scoreboard stock forced up right before intermission.
	LUINotifyEvent( &"force_scoreboard", 1, 0 );

	// THE MENU: flip AetheriumStartMenu into its two-entry mode, re-enable the
	// ingame menu, force it open on everyone.
	SetDvar( "tod_go_active", "1" );
	SetMatchFlag( "disableIngameMenu", 0 );
	wait 0.1;   // let the dvar land before the menu's createMenu reads it
	players = GetPlayers();
	for ( i = 0; i < players.size; i++ )
	{
		if ( isdefined( players[ i ] ) && isplayer( players[ i ] ) )
			players[ i ] OpenMenu( "StartMenu_Main" );
	}

	// Both choices act from the menu (map_restart / disconnect tear the VM
	// down mid-wait — the intended exits). This only completes with NO choice.
	wait TOD_GO_DECIDE_SECS;
	level.tod_go_done = true;   // stands the failsafe down
	ExitLevel( false );         // the stock terminal call
}

// LAST-RESORT EXIT WATCHDOG: fully independent of the main flow — if no
// decision landed by now (main thread errored/died), exit exactly like stock.
function gameover_failsafe()
{
	level waittill( "end_game" );
	wait TOD_GO_FAILSAFE_SECS;
	if ( IS_TRUE( level.tod_go_done ) )
		return;
	ExitLevel( false );
}
